{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And they stood beside the cows</b> — at their side and close to them, and it is a sign that there would be no interruption between the seven years of plenty and the seven years of famine, even though he did not tell this to Joseph. Or perhaps the vision and the account were identical, and Scripture does not bother, just as it added in the account 'and it could not be known that they had come inside them' (Genesis 41:21), and likewise 'going up on one stalk' (Genesis 41:5) — a sign that they would be seven consecutive years:"], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 41, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:43:33.311422036Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}